# 28. The Agent Loop

A useful abstraction for an AI social media agent is:

```text
while goal_not_complete:

    observe()

    update_state()

    reason()

    plan_next_step()

    select_tool()

    validate_action()

    execute()

    record_result()

    evaluate()
```

The actual implementation may use a framework, custom orchestration layer, workflow engine, or another architecture.

The important concept is the feedback loop.

A fixed automation script generally follows a predetermined path.

An agent can use the result of one operation to determine what should happen next.

---

# 29. Example: Autonomous Content Campaign

Suppose the objective is:

```text
Run this week's content campaign.
```

The agent might execute:

```text
1. Inspect campaign configuration
2. Read available content
3. Identify approved assets
4. Review previous performance
5. Select suitable content
6. Generate platform-specific metadata
7. Validate content
8. Select target accounts
9. Generate distribution tasks
10. Schedule tasks
11. Monitor execution
12. Collect results
13. Produce campaign report
```

The system becomes a continuous workflow rather than a collection of disconnected automation actions.

